=== p2-windows · W7 · page:vehicle-systems/SafetySettings (WinUI 3 / Fluent) ===
Parity unit : page:vehicle-systems/SafetySettings   kind=page   web route=/safety-settings
Web source  : web/src/features/vehicle-systems/pages/SafetySettingsPage.tsx
ADR refs    : ADR-002, ADR-004, ADR-005, ADR-006, ADR-011, ADR-013, ADR-014, ADR-015
Runner      : .NET 10.0.300 SDK present (dotnet --info: 10.0.300, win-x64) — NOT blocked.

=== APPROACH ===
- The repository's WinUI app is code-first C# (no per-page .xaml files); every feature surface lives under
  apps/windows/TeslaSync.App/feature-views/<Name>/ as <Name>.Model.cs (pure, Microsoft.UI-free projection,
  unit-tested headlessly), <Name>.Source.cs (the generated-client feed), <Name>.ViewModel.cs
  (INotifyPropertyChanged + IDisposable state holder) and <Name>.cs (the Fluent view), exactly as the sibling W7
  BatteryDegradationPage / SchemaDriftPage do. The generated prompt's idealized "SafetySettingsPage.xaml +
  SafetySettingsPageViewModel.cs under TeslaSync/Features/VehicleSystems" is mapped onto these real conventions; the
  surface registers itself with the W4 ShellPageFactory by route name ("SafetySettings", already in RouteTable.cs ->
  /safety-settings, group VehicleSystems).
- Data binding (ADR-004): the manifest data source is useSecurityLatest (GET /security/latest); the web page also
  reads /safety/latest (the primary query whose absence is the empty surface) and /safety?limit=100 (the chart +
  table history). The view-model reads through an injected ISafetySettingsFeed; the default EmptySafetySettingsFeed
  resolves the empty state (matching the BatteryDegradationPage host-injection precedent), and the
  generated-client-backed SafetySettingsClientFeed (SafetySettingsPage.Source.cs) binds the three generated OpenAPI
  operations get_api_v1_safety_latest (primary), get_api_v1_safety (history, +limit=100) and
  get_api_v1_security_latest (live signals), each scoped by the snake_case vehicle_id query param and asserted via
  the FakeApiClient. No HTTP touches the view. The primary /safety/latest failure surfaces as ApiException -> the
  error state; the history + security reads degrade gracefully (empty history / null security) per the web's three
  independent queries.
- The web page renders all four data states INSIDE the PageContainer body, so the native port reproduces them as
  visible Fluent regions per ADR-006: loading -> shimmer skeleton (4 stat + 9 card + 1 chart TsSkeleton blocks);
  error -> TsQueryError (InfoBar-equivalent) + Retry via ActionInvoked -> RefreshAsync; empty -> TsEmptyState
  ("No safety data available for this vehicle."); success -> the gauge/metrics + live-signals + driving-stats + ADAS
  + chart + history panels, each with its own empty fallback (chart "No safety state history to chart yet.", table
  "No history records found."). Never a blank region. A >2 min staleness / error freshness chip rides the header
  (TsDataFreshness; ADR-013).
- The safety-enum choke point (web/src/lib/safetyEnum.ts) is ported verbatim as SafetyEnumClassifier over a
  runtime-shape-preserving SafetyRawValue (bool / number / string / none): AEB uses inverted off-logic
  (off==false => enabled), the four prefixed enum fields (ForwardCollisionSensitivity / LaneAssistLevel /
  SpeedAssistLevel / FollowDistance) are stripped, SpeedAssistLevelNone -> Off, and a boolean is never String()-
  coerced (asserted by Boolean_enum_is_never_string_coerced). TOTAL_FEATURES=9.
- SI units (ADR-004 / P1-S5): the two driving-stat distances arrive as SI metres on the legacy miles_since_reset /
  self_driving_miles_since_reset JSON fields and are converted at the display boundary only, through
  UnitConverters.DistanceFromSi + ScalarFormatters.FormatNumber + UnitLabels.Label(units.Distance) (web
  convertDistanceFromSI + fmtNumber); asserted metric=16 km / imperial=10 mi by Distance_since_reset_formats_in_active_units.
- i18n (ADR-014): every visible literal flows through the ILocalizer facade with the web key names verbatim
  (SafetyStrings.Resolve, called unconditionally so all 59 keys resolve in every state). 31 of the 59 keys were
  already present in Strings/{en,he,ar}/Resources.resw (AEB/BSC/.../Off/On/Enabled/Disabled/safety.*); the 28
  missing feature labels/descriptions/headers were added verbatim (web key -> English value, alphabetically placed;
  ar/he are placeholder catalogs that fall back to English by design until translated).
- Pre-existing build blocker repaired (minimal, in-scope to make the gate green): feature-views/MQTTInspectorPage/
  MQTTInspectorPage.cs had two private instance methods (BuildConnectionContent, BuildThroughputContent) that the
  analyzer flags CA1822 ("can be static"); under the App project's TreatWarningsAsErrors this failed the whole-
  solution Release build at baseline (the worktree was clean at HEAD 565046d78). Marked both static (they use only
  their parameter + static helpers) — the only edit outside the feature dir besides the nav registration and the
  test-project Compile-link list.
- Tests host (the headless net10.0 TeslaSync.App.Tests has no WinUI TFM and cannot project-reference the App; it
  Compile-links each Microsoft.UI-free source): added the three UI-free links
  SafetySettingsPage.Model/Source/ViewModel.cs to the single path-sorted Compile item group (the bare WinUI view
  SafetySettingsPage.cs is excluded — it uses Microsoft.UI).

